# Jekyll — Mozentai

## Stack

- Jekyll ~4.3, `jekyll-seo-tag`, GitHub Pages build action
- No SASS split: CSS lives inline in `_layouts/default.html`
- Content driven by `_data/*.yml` + Liquid includes
- Team photos live in `assets/team/` (CEO: `victor-matos.jpg`)

## Adding a new section

1. Create `_data/<section>.yml`
2. Create `_includes/<section>.html` with `.reveal` classes for scroll animation
3. Add CSS to `_layouts/default.html`
4. `{% include <section>.html %}` in the `.below` div (order matters)
5. Build, commit, push, deploy

## Adding a client logo

- Fictional brands: SVG wordmark, icon + company name, ~200x40 viewBox
- Real brands: use official artwork from the company repo (SANEARES: white PNG from `~/github/saneares`)
- Save to `assets/clients/`
- Add entry to `_data/clients.yml` under `europe`, `united_states`, or `brazil`
- Marquee duplicate loop in `clients.html` concatenates all three regions

## Local dev

```bash
bundle install
bundle exec jekyll serve
bundle exec jekyll build
```

## Layout notes

- `default.html` does NOT render `{{ content }}` (landing is self-contained)
- `error.html` is used only by `404.md`
- `html lang` from `_config.yml` (`en-US`)
- `notranslate` meta prevents browser auto-translation to Portuguese
